  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Mission Systems obligated $577M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Mission Systems received 38 awards so far, with an average award size of $15.2M, and obligations are up 64.4% year over year. Obligations grew from $351M in FY25 to $577M in FY26. Engineering Services is the dominant market, with obligations of $535M in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Mission Systems also shows smaller obligations across several other NAICS categories, including Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $15.6M and Security Systems Services at $13.6M. Historical annual obligations include $379M in FY21, $336M in FY22, $357M in FY23, $430M in FY24, and $351M in FY25. The FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial. This snapshot highlights where current federal spending is concentrated and the scale of awards received so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large are General Dynamics Mission Systems' federal obligations in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Mission Systems obligated $577M in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Mission Systems received 38 awards so far, with an average award size of $15.2M, and obligations are up 64.4% year over year. General Dynamics Mission Systems' annual obligations were $379M in FY21, $336M in FY22, $357M in FY23, $430M in FY24, and $351M in FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do General Dynamics Mission Systems' FY2026 obligations go by market?",
        "body": "Engineering Services received $535M of obligations in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Mission Systems also had obligations in Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment (except Automotive and Electronic) Repair and Maintenance at $15.6M, Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) at $13.6M, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $7.7M. Smaller market obligations include Software Publishers at $143K and Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $96.1K."
      }
    ]
  },
